  %% Algorithm: the reversible point-add construction
  Phases["Affine P plus Q in eight in-place phases: x -= Qx, y -= Qy, y /= x gives lambda, x += 3Qx, x -= lambda squared, y *= x, y -= Qy, x = Qx - x"]
  Coord["Coordinate blocks from Gold1298: classical-offset subtract, add 3Qx, final subtract and reverse subtract"]
  Square["Modular square from Gold1298: Karatsuba down to 64-bit schoolbook triangles, folded with the signed digits of f = 2^32 + 977"]
  DivLeg["Division leg: seed rails from x, P1 = y/2, 150 fused ticks (rails tick then payload tick), endpoint, rails walk back"]
  MulLeg["Multiplication leg: rails-only forward walk, endpoint payload (s0 y, s1 y), 150 fused reverse ticks, clear P1 = P0/2"]
  Walk["Leapfrog walk: two odd signed rails; per tick two forced add-halves, a deep or flat choice add-halve, then 0 to 3 extra halvings"]
  Choice["Choice rule: deep if tz of the deep sum is 3 or 4, flat if 5 or more, else a sign test or a 22-bit magnitude window compare"]
  Tape["History tape: one 5-bit letter per tick; the tick-0 letter is recomputed from the low 7 bits of R1 and erased early"]
  Cells["Payload cells: P_i = mu R_i mod p; three signed modular add-halve cells per tick, chosen by free room"]
  Rot["Extra shift: rotr_e(W) = (W + h(f-1)) 2^-e mod p; 80-bit fold, then three controlled reflections"]
  Cleanup["Cleanup: at the endpoint the rails are plus or minus 1, so one payload is cleared against the other; reversing the walk consumes the tape and restores x; every phase returns scratch to zero"]

